     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or about 850 mg three times daily. It is also above the 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day maximum for extended-release. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity rises substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you have in mind\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily as written, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was confirmed intentionally. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
